<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Franceville</h1><p class="st-meta">1889 CE – 1890 CE · capital Franceville</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived self-governing commune at Port Vila in the New Hebrides, often said to be the first polity with universal suffrage regardless of sex or race.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1887 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> agreed that neither would annex the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-hebrides-condominium">New Hebrides</a>, leaving the islands without any government over the settlers. In 1889 residents of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-vila">Port Vila</a> area, mostly French settlers linked to the Société Française des Nouvelles-Hébrides, declared an independent municipality called Franceville.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its charter gave the vote to all adult residents, men and women, without regard to race, though only white men could hold office. It had a small elected council and an elected president, and it relied on the goodwill of planters and traders in a population of a few hundred Europeans and many more ni-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a>. Little is recorded of its day-to-day administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, unwilling to accept an independent settler state, refused to recognise it, and the commune collapsed in 1890. The islands later came under joint rule as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-hebrides-condominium">New Hebrides Condominium</a>, and the site is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-vila">Port Vila</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1889 CE – 1890 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.29%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1889 CE – 1890 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Franceville</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism, Indigenous religions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, English, Bislama</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Vanuatu</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Commune of Franceville</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=republic-of-franceville" aria-label="Republic of Franceville on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="9237 2749 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Franceville lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9557 3005h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M9557 3005h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Vanuatu. <a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=republic-of-franceville">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

